  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7560214a2c335bd4e9cc29951d82c1e3, type: 3}
  m_Name: Guevara
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCInfoSO
  npcID: lieutenant_guevara
  displayName: Lieutenant Guevara
  characterFullName: Miguel Guevarra
  alias: Teniente Guevara
  characterCategory: Military / Civil Guard Officer
  portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b45d037ab671a154da17833d44f3223e, type: 3}
  description: An elderly lieutenant of the Civil Guard with a stern appearance and
    a direct manner of speaking. Unlike many of the guests, he openly defends the
    honor of Don Rafael Ibarra.
  biography: "Lieutenant Guevara is an old officer of the Civil Guard who knew Don
    Rafael Ibarra personally. At Capit\xE1n Tiago\u2019s gathering, he challenges
    Fray D\xE1maso\u2019s account of the controversy surrounding Don Rafael\u2019s
    burial. Guevara describes Don Rafael as an honorable and worthy man and condemns
    the removal of his body from the cemetery. When Cris\xF3stomo arrives, the lieutenant
    welcomes him warmly and becomes emotional while speaking about his father."
  characterFacts:
  - He is an officer of the Civil Guard.
  - He is described as tall, elderly and austere.
  - He speaks in a harsh, brief and direct manner.
  - He knew Don Rafael Ibarra personally.
  - He considers Don Rafael one of the worthiest men in the Philippines.
  - He rejects the claim that Don Rafael committed suicide.
  - "He shows sympathy toward Cris\xF3stomo Ibarra."
  introductionLines:
  - Lieutenant Guevara, of the Civil Guard.
  - I speak plainly, and I expect others to do the same.
  repeatDialogues:
  - lines:
    - Rank and authority must still answer to justice.
    - I will not remain silent when an honorable man is slandered.
